## 5. `impl Iterator` / `impl Trait` Return Type

`memory.rs:42`

```rust
fn usable_frames(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = PhysFrame> {
    let regions = self.memory_map.iter();
    let usable_regions = regions.filter(...);
    let addr_ranges = usable_regions.map(...);
    let frame_addresses = addr_ranges.flat_map(...);
    frame_addresses.map(...)
}
```

Returns an opaque iterator type without naming the full chained iterator type (which would be
unwriteable). Each combinator creates a new anonymous type; `impl Iterator` lets you return the
whole chain without boxing it. Compare to `Box<dyn Iterator>` which heap-allocates — `impl Trait`
is zero-cost.

