## 6. `Option<&'static mut T>` as a Safe Linked List Node

`allocator/linked_list.rs:31-35`

```rust
struct ListNode {
    size: usize,
    next: Option<&'static mut ListNode>,
}
```

A linked list in unsafe Rust usually uses raw pointers (`*mut`). Using `Option<&'static mut
ListNode>` instead encodes nullability in the type (`None` = no next node) and preserves aliasing
rules — `&'static mut` is an exclusive reference. The `'static` lifetime says the node lives in
the heap for the program's lifetime. Study how `node.next.take()` is used to move out of the
option and break the chain safely.

