## 7. Atomic Operations for Lock-Free State

`task/mod.rs:34`

```rust
static NEXT_ID: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
TaskId(NEXT_ID.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed))
```

`fetch_add` atomically increments and returns the old value — no lock needed. `Ordering::Relaxed`
is sufficient here because the IDs just need to be unique, not ordered relative to other memory
operations. Know the difference between `Relaxed`, `Acquire`, `Release`, and `SeqCst`.

