## 8. `Arc<T>` + `Wake` Trait for Waker Implementation

`task/executor.rs:76-101`

```rust
struct TaskWaker {
    task_id: TaskId,
    task_queue: Arc<ArrayQueue<TaskId>>,
}

impl Wake for TaskWaker {
    fn wake(self: Arc<Self>) {
        self.wake_task();
    }
}
```

`Waker` requires the type to be clonable (it may be stored and fired from multiple places).
`Arc<TaskWaker>` provides shared ownership across the executor and any external interrupt handler
that holds a clone. `Wake` is implemented on `Arc<Self>` specifically —
`Waker::from(Arc::new(TaskWaker {...}))` converts it. This is the canonical pattern for custom
async runtimes.

