## 10. Atomic Enable-and-Halt for Idle Sleep

`task/executor.rs:64-72`

```rust
fn sleep_if_idle(&self) {
    interrupts::disable();
    if self.task_queue.is_empty() {
        enable_and_hlt();   // atomic: enables interrupts AND halts in one step
    } else {
        interrupts::enable();
    }
}
```

`enable_and_hlt()` is a single CPU instruction sequence that prevents a wake-up from being missed.
If you did `enable(); hlt();` separately, an interrupt could fire between the two — the task queue
gets populated, `wake()` fires, but the CPU hasn't halted yet and the wakeup is lost. The CPU
then halts and waits forever. This is a hardware-level race condition and `enable_and_hlt` is the
correct fix.

